[{"text": "The assembly will hear an address by his", "start": 5.279, "duration": 7.121}, {"text": "excellency Julius Mada Bon, president of", "start": 8.32, "duration": 8.12}, {"text": "the Republic of Serillion.", "start": 12.4, "duration": 4.04}, {"text": "I request protocol to escort his", "start": 16.72, "duration": 5.68}, {"text": "excellency and invite him to address the", "start": 19.279, "duration": 6.121}, {"text": "assembly.", "start": 22.4, "duration": 3.0}, {"text": "Mr. President of the General Assembly,", "start": 41.12, "duration": 7.919}, {"text": "Mr. Secretary General,", "start": 45.6, "duration": 5.84}, {"text": "Excellencies, distinguished ladies and", "start": 49.039, "duration": 5.401}, {"text": "gentlemen,", "start": 51.44, "duration": 3.0}, {"text": "I congratulate his excellency Khalil", "start": 54.8, "duration": 4.64}, {"text": "Raman", "start": 57.68, "duration": 5.519}, {"text": "on his election as president of the 81st", "start": 59.44, "duration": 8.359}, {"text": "session of the General Assembly.", "start": 63.199, "duration": 4.6}, {"text": "President Raman assumes this", "start": 68.0, "duration": 5.119}, {"text": "responsibility at a moment that demands", "start": 70.08, "duration": 7.52}, {"text": "principled and steady leadership.", "start": 73.119, "duration": 9.441}, {"text": "He has Syrian's full support.", "start": 77.6, "duration": 8.0}, {"text": "I pay tribute to his excellency", "start": 82.56, "duration": 6.32}, {"text": "secretary general Antonio Gutirez", "start": 85.6, "duration": 5.36}, {"text": "who is in the closing months of his", "start": 88.88, "duration": 4.559}, {"text": "mandate.", "start": 90.96, "duration": 5.92}, {"text": "He has served this organization with", "start": 93.439, "duration": 5.761}, {"text": "steadfastness,", "start": 96.88, "duration": 4.72}, {"text": "moral clarity", "start": 99.2, "duration": 6.239}, {"text": "and the courage to speak", "start": 101.6, "duration": 6.559}, {"text": "difficult truths.", "start": 105.439, "duration": 5.601}, {"text": "I also commend her excellency Amina J.", "start": 108.159, "duration": 4.721}, {"text": "Muhammad,", "start": 111.04, "duration": 5.119}, {"text": "the deputy secretary general, for her", "start": 112.88, "duration": 6.239}, {"text": "exemplary service and distinguished", "start": 116.159, "duration": 6.56}, {"text": "representation of Africa on the global", "start": 119.119, "duration": 6.6}, {"text": "stage.", "start": 122.719, "duration": 3.0}, {"text": "Mr. President,", "start": 128.0, "duration": 6.0}, {"text": "nearly 25 years ago,", "start": 130.959, "duration": 6.561}, {"text": "Srielon completed disarmament and", "start": 134.0, "duration": 9.319}, {"text": "formally declared its civil war over.", "start": 137.52, "duration": 5.799}, {"text": "The former declaration matters, of", "start": 143.84, "duration": 6.08}, {"text": "course, but peace became rare in more", "start": 145.84, "duration": 7.28}, {"text": "practical ways.", "start": 149.92, "duration": 6.56}, {"text": "In the families that returned home,", "start": 153.12, "duration": 6.0}, {"text": "in the communities that learned to live", "start": 156.48, "duration": 5.039}, {"text": "together again,", "start": 159.12, "duration": 5.92}, {"text": "in the citizens who chose the ballot,", "start": 161.519, "duration": 5.601}, {"text": "and in institutions", "start": 165.04, "duration": 5.36}, {"text": "that slowly returned back", "start": 167.12, "duration": 6.6}, {"text": "to confidence,", "start": 170.4, "duration": 3.32}, {"text": "the United Nations", "start": 174.4, "duration": 5.919}, {"text": "stood with us through disarmament,", "start": 176.64, "duration": 5.2}, {"text": "election,", "start": 180.319, "duration": 6.761}, {"text": "and the long work of peace building.", "start": 181.84, "duration": 5.24}, {"text": "So we know what international", "start": 187.12, "duration": 5.68}, {"text": "cooperation can make possible because we", "start": 189.04, "duration": 7.479}, {"text": "have lived it.", "start": 192.8, "duration": 3.719}, {"text": "The experience taught us that trust", "start": 196.8, "duration": 7.519}, {"text": "cannot be commanded by declaration.", "start": 199.519, "duration": 9.281}, {"text": "Trust grows when promises are honored.", "start": 204.319, "duration": 7.521}, {"text": "When the law protects everyone. when", "start": 208.8, "duration": 4.88}, {"text": "institutions", "start": 211.84, "duration": 5.2}, {"text": "serve their people and when citizens can", "start": 213.68, "duration": 8.119}, {"text": "see a future for themselves.", "start": 217.04, "duration": 4.759}, {"text": "Serum brings that lesson to this", "start": 222.0, "duration": 5.44}, {"text": "assembly at a moment when trust between", "start": 224.48, "duration": 6.319}, {"text": "nations in institutions and in", "start": 227.44, "duration": 6.48}, {"text": "multilateral cooperation is under", "start": 230.799, "duration": 7.201}, {"text": "profound strain.", "start": 233.92, "duration": 7.12}, {"text": "In this year's theme,", "start": 238.0, "duration": 5.439}, {"text": "restoring trust, managing", "start": 241.04, "duration": 3.919}, {"text": "transformation,", "start": 243.439, "duration": 5.601}, {"text": "a united nation that delivers for all.", "start": 244.959, "duration": 6.161}, {"text": "The words", "start": 249.04, "duration": 8.68}, {"text": "for all carry its defining moral weight.", "start": 251.12, "duration": 6.6}, {"text": "The words for all ask not only whether", "start": 257.84, "duration": 5.28}, {"text": "United Nations can act", "start": 260.4, "duration": 4.64}, {"text": "but also", "start": 263.12, "duration": 5.12}, {"text": "its actions", "start": 265.04, "duration": 6.64}, {"text": "where they reach", "start": 268.24, "duration": 6.0}, {"text": "whose voices shape them and whose", "start": 271.68, "duration": 6.84}, {"text": "dignity they protect.", "start": 274.24, "duration": 4.28}, {"text": "An institution may act quickly and still", "start": 278.56, "duration": 8.56}, {"text": "fail those it was meant to serve.", "start": 281.6, "duration": 8.72}, {"text": "Delivery worthy of the UN charter must", "start": 287.12, "duration": 6.48}, {"text": "reach those farthest from power and", "start": 290.32, "duration": 5.84}, {"text": "recognize the equal worth of every", "start": 293.6, "duration": 7.76}, {"text": "nation and every human life.", "start": 296.16, "duration": 8.16}, {"text": "This is the standard by which the world", "start": 301.36, "duration": 6.08}, {"text": "will judge us all.", "start": 304.32, "duration": 5.439}, {"text": "Mr. President,", "start": 307.44, "duration": 6.479}, {"text": "that standard begins with trust.", "start": 309.759, "duration": 6.561}, {"text": "Trust is the currency of", "start": 313.919, "duration": 5.401}, {"text": "multilateralism.", "start": 316.32, "duration": 3.0}, {"text": "Trust is gained when the law protects", "start": 319.52, "duration": 6.32}, {"text": "the vulnerable as firmly as it restrains", "start": 322.24, "duration": 6.72}, {"text": "the powerful.", "start": 325.84, "duration": 6.24}, {"text": "International law must not change with", "start": 328.96, "duration": 6.239}, {"text": "geography or bend according to the", "start": 332.08, "duration": 6.88}, {"text": "identity of the accused.", "start": 335.199, "duration": 6.0}, {"text": "In the Middle East,", "start": 338.96, "duration": 5.28}, {"text": "the UN charter and international law", "start": 341.199, "duration": 7.401}, {"text": "must guide must guide us.", "start": 344.24, "duration": 4.36}, {"text": "Civilians must be protected,", "start": 352.639, "duration": 6.56}, {"text": "humanitarian access ensured, aggression", "start": 355.44, "duration": 6.88}, {"text": "and occupation ended, and freedom of", "start": 359.199, "duration": 6.481}, {"text": "navigation safeguarded.", "start": 362.32, "duration": 6.159}, {"text": "The inalienable right of the Palestinian", "start": 365.68, "duration": 5.44}, {"text": "people to self-determination", "start": 368.479, "duration": 6.321}, {"text": "must be realized", "start": 371.12, "duration": 7.04}, {"text": "through a viable", "start": 374.8, "duration": 6.0}, {"text": "state of Palestine living alongside the", "start": 378.16, "duration": 5.2}, {"text": "state of Israel in peace and in", "start": 380.8, "duration": 4.959}, {"text": "security.", "start": 383.36, "duration": 4.959}, {"text": "That same commitment to peace requires", "start": 385.759, "duration": 5.361}, {"text": "progress on nuclear disarmament and", "start": 388.319, "duration": 6.241}, {"text": "nonprololiferation through diplomacy.", "start": 391.12, "duration": 6.96}, {"text": "In Sudan, civilians continue to endure", "start": 394.56, "duration": 8.4}, {"text": "endure atrocities and displacement,", "start": 398.08, "duration": 8.72}, {"text": "underscoring the cost of delayed action.", "start": 402.96, "duration": 6.72}, {"text": "Syrial calls for their protection,", "start": 406.8, "duration": 6.08}, {"text": "unhindered humanitarian access,", "start": 409.68, "duration": 5.04}, {"text": "accountability,", "start": 412.88, "duration": 4.879}, {"text": "and a Sudaneseled political process that", "start": 414.72, "duration": 6.0}, {"text": "safeguards the country's sovereignty,", "start": 417.759, "duration": 7.88}, {"text": "unity, and territorial integrity.", "start": 420.72, "duration": 4.919}, {"text": "In the Eastern Democratic Republic of", "start": 427.039, "duration": 4.641}, {"text": "the Congo,", "start": 429.36, "duration": 4.8}, {"text": "agreements have not yet silenced the", "start": 431.68, "duration": 7.2}, {"text": "guns or allowed millions to return home.", "start": 434.16, "duration": 8.24}, {"text": "Across West Africa and the Saher,", "start": 438.88, "duration": 7.2}, {"text": "terrorism feeds on poverty, exclusion,", "start": 442.4, "duration": 8.239}, {"text": "unemployment, and weak institutions.", "start": 446.08, "duration": 8.0}, {"text": "These conflicts differ in origin and", "start": 450.639, "duration": 5.041}, {"text": "circumstance,", "start": 454.08, "duration": 6.72}, {"text": "but they carry a common warning.", "start": 455.68, "duration": 8.079}, {"text": "Military action may contain a threat,", "start": 460.8, "duration": 6.48}, {"text": "but it cannot by itself build lasting", "start": 463.759, "duration": 6.241}, {"text": "peace.", "start": 467.28, "duration": 5.68}, {"text": "When hunger, exclusion, and despair", "start": 470.0, "duration": 7.919}, {"text": "deepen, insecurity takes root.", "start": 472.96, "duration": 6.88}, {"text": "The connection between peace and", "start": 477.919, "duration": 5.12}, {"text": "development must therefore move from our", "start": 479.84, "duration": 7.52}, {"text": "resolutions into our budgets.", "start": 483.039, "duration": 6.72}, {"text": "In 2025,", "start": 487.36, "duration": 4.8}, {"text": "global military expenditure reached", "start": 489.759, "duration": 4.801}, {"text": "about 2.9", "start": 492.16, "duration": 6.4}, {"text": "trillion United State dollars, the 11th", "start": 494.56, "duration": 8.639}, {"text": "consecutive annual increase.", "start": 498.56, "duration": 6.72}, {"text": "Of course, nations have legitimate", "start": 503.199, "duration": 4.481}, {"text": "security needs.", "start": 505.28, "duration": 4.8}, {"text": "But the speed with which the world finds", "start": 507.68, "duration": 5.52}, {"text": "resources for war", "start": 510.08, "duration": 6.72}, {"text": "compared to prevention and development", "start": 513.2, "duration": 6.6}, {"text": "reveal", "start": 516.8, "duration": 3.0}, {"text": "law also depends on who has the voice in", "start": 527.92, "duration": 7.039}, {"text": "applying it.", "start": 532.56, "duration": 4.24}, {"text": "The credibility weakens when", "start": 534.959, "duration": 4.961}, {"text": "institutions entrusted with the law", "start": 536.8, "duration": 6.0}, {"text": "preserve an unequal distribution of", "start": 539.92, "duration": 5.44}, {"text": "power.", "start": 542.8, "duration": 5.039}, {"text": "The Security Council still reflects the", "start": 545.36, "duration": 6.12}, {"text": "world of 1945.", "start": 547.839, "duration": 3.641}, {"text": "Africa, home to more than 1.6 billion", "start": 551.519, "duration": 6.641}, {"text": "people and the subject of most of the", "start": 555.04, "duration": 6.239}, {"text": "council's work, still has no permanent", "start": 558.16, "duration": 5.679}, {"text": "seat.", "start": 561.279, "duration": 5.68}, {"text": "That's not fair.", "start": 563.839, "duration": 5.68}, {"text": "Africa seeks its rightful place because", "start": 566.959, "duration": 6.241}, {"text": "the council cannot be fully legitimate", "start": 569.519, "duration": 7.681}, {"text": "or effective while an entire continent", "start": 573.2, "duration": 8.759}, {"text": "remains permanently absent", "start": 577.2, "duration": 4.759}, {"text": "from its highest level of decision", "start": 582.8, "duration": 4.96}, {"text": "making.", "start": 585.6, "duration": 6.799}, {"text": "No durable global solution on peace,", "start": 587.76, "duration": 8.88}, {"text": "climate, food, energy or technology can", "start": 592.399, "duration": 8.961}, {"text": "be built without African leadership.", "start": 596.64, "duration": 7.84}, {"text": "The common African position espoused in", "start": 601.36, "duration": 6.72}, {"text": "Ezinia consensus and such declaration", "start": 604.48, "duration": 5.919}, {"text": "calls for no fewer than two permanent", "start": 608.08, "duration": 5.28}, {"text": "seats with all the rights and privileges", "start": 610.399, "duration": 6.641}, {"text": "of permanent membership including the", "start": 613.36, "duration": 7.12}, {"text": "veto if it is retained and five", "start": 617.04, "duration": 7.44}, {"text": "non-permanent seats.", "start": 620.48, "duration": 7.599}, {"text": "As coordinator of the African Union", "start": 624.48, "duration": 7.28}, {"text": "Committee of 10, Syria will continue to", "start": 628.079, "duration": 7.88}, {"text": "advance that position.", "start": 631.76, "duration": 4.199}, {"text": "Years of intergovernmental negotiation", "start": 636.64, "duration": 5.84}, {"text": "without realizing the reform has tested", "start": 639.36, "duration": 7.36}, {"text": "the credibility of the process.", "start": 642.48, "duration": 7.039}, {"text": "Before this session concludes,", "start": 646.72, "duration": 5.2}, {"text": "member states should have a consolidated", "start": 649.519, "duration": 4.56}, {"text": "model", "start": 651.92, "duration": 4.32}, {"text": "which we committed", "start": 654.079, "duration": 7.681}, {"text": "to in the past for the future.", "start": 656.24, "duration": 7.76}, {"text": "Sri speaks", "start": 661.76, "duration": 5.28}, {"text": "with the authority of service.", "start": 664.0, "duration": 5.279}, {"text": "During our time on the security council", "start": 667.04, "duration": 5.12}, {"text": "in 2024 2025,", "start": 669.279, "duration": 6.8}, {"text": "we worked as a voice of reason and a", "start": 672.16, "duration": 6.72}, {"text": "bridge across division.", "start": 676.079, "duration": 5.281}, {"text": "We convened the Security Council's first", "start": 678.88, "duration": 5.68}, {"text": "high level debate on redressing", "start": 681.36, "duration": 7.44}, {"text": "historical injustice against Africa,", "start": 684.56, "duration": 7.36}, {"text": "placed conflict related food insecurity", "start": 688.8, "duration": 6.24}, {"text": "at the center of its agenda,", "start": 691.92, "duration": 7.12}, {"text": "and with Guyana co-drafted unanimously", "start": 695.04, "duration": 7.6}, {"text": "adopted resolution 2807", "start": 699.04, "duration": 7.76}, {"text": "on youth peace and security,", "start": 702.64, "duration": 6.8}, {"text": "strengthening young people's role in", "start": 706.8, "duration": 7.96}, {"text": "conflict prevention and peace building.", "start": 709.44, "duration": 5.32}, {"text": "Mr. President,", "start": 715.36, "duration": 3.32}, {"text": "representation becomes meaningful when", "start": 719.04, "duration": 7.2}, {"text": "it changes decisions and improves lives.", "start": 721.12, "duration": 7.36}, {"text": "The imbalance within the security", "start": 726.24, "duration": 5.599}, {"text": "council is also present in international", "start": 728.48, "duration": 6.64}, {"text": "financial institutions whose structures", "start": 731.839, "duration": 5.921}, {"text": "still bear the imprint of an earlier", "start": 735.12, "duration": 5.6}, {"text": "age.", "start": 737.76, "duration": 5.199}, {"text": "Developing countries need fairer voting", "start": 740.72, "duration": 5.44}, {"text": "power, stronger representation and", "start": 742.959, "duration": 5.281}, {"text": "increased capital within these", "start": 746.16, "duration": 5.76}, {"text": "institutions together with affordable", "start": 748.24, "duration": 6.719}, {"text": "finance, concessional resources and", "start": 751.92, "duration": 7.359}, {"text": "fairer debt treatment.", "start": 754.959, "duration": 6.641}, {"text": "They must also participate equally in", "start": 759.279, "duration": 4.721}, {"text": "shaping the rules of international", "start": 761.6, "duration": 4.64}, {"text": "taxation.", "start": 764.0, "duration": 5.36}, {"text": "Srielion therefore supports", "start": 766.24, "duration": 5.76}, {"text": "a UN framework convention on", "start": 769.36, "duration": 6.479}, {"text": "international tax cooperation", "start": 772.0, "duration": 6.24}, {"text": "through Echos", "start": 775.839, "duration": 4.881}, {"text": "serum we champion a development system", "start": 778.24, "duration": 5.76}, {"text": "that responds more effectively to", "start": 780.72, "duration": 7.64}, {"text": "Africa's priorities.", "start": 784.0, "duration": 4.36}, {"text": "Mr. President,", "start": 788.639, "duration": 5.44}, {"text": "restoring trust", "start": 791.519, "duration": 5.201}, {"text": "and delivering for all must also embrace", "start": 794.079, "duration": 5.44}, {"text": "the unfinished cause of reparatory", "start": 796.72, "duration": 5.359}, {"text": "justice.", "start": 799.519, "duration": 4.641}, {"text": "In March,", "start": 802.079, "duration": 6.241}, {"text": "this assembly adopted a resolution led", "start": 804.16, "duration": 7.04}, {"text": "by Ghana and supported by the African", "start": 808.32, "duration": 6.56}, {"text": "Union and Caribbean community", "start": 811.2, "duration": 5.68}, {"text": "recognizing the trafficking and", "start": 814.88, "duration": 4.959}, {"text": "racialized charter enslavement of", "start": 816.88, "duration": 6.48}, {"text": "Africans as the gravest crime against", "start": 819.839, "duration": 6.521}, {"text": "humanity.", "start": 823.36, "duration": 3.0}, {"text": "For Sriraillon,", "start": 826.959, "duration": 5.201}, {"text": "this history is neither abstract nor", "start": 829.6, "duration": 4.479}, {"text": "distant.", "start": 832.16, "duration": 5.119}, {"text": "From Bones Island in our own river", "start": 834.079, "duration": 7.041}, {"text": "estuary, thousands of Africans were", "start": 837.279, "duration": 7.441}, {"text": "forcibly transported across the Atlantic", "start": 841.12, "duration": 6.719}, {"text": "into enslavement.", "start": 844.72, "duration": 5.76}, {"text": "Freetown, our capital, would later", "start": 847.839, "duration": 6.401}, {"text": "become a home for formerly enslaved and", "start": 850.48, "duration": 7.76}, {"text": "liberated Africans.", "start": 854.24, "duration": 7.68}, {"text": "This history is woven into our national", "start": 858.24, "duration": 5.76}, {"text": "identity.", "start": 861.92, "duration": 3.599}, {"text": "However,", "start": 864.0, "duration": 3.839}, {"text": "the consequences did not end with", "start": 865.519, "duration": 5.12}, {"text": "abolition.", "start": 867.839, "duration": 7.201}, {"text": "Their legacy continues to be reflected", "start": 870.639, "duration": 8.081}, {"text": "in enduring disparities in wealth,", "start": 875.04, "duration": 9.12}, {"text": "power, and opportunity across our world.", "start": 878.72, "duration": 8.08}, {"text": "Reparatory justice is therefore not a", "start": 884.16, "duration": 6.08}, {"text": "plea for charity. It is a call for", "start": 886.8, "duration": 5.039}, {"text": "acknowledgment,", "start": 890.24, "duration": 4.88}, {"text": "former apology, the return of cultural", "start": 891.839, "duration": 4.881}, {"text": "heritage,", "start": 895.12, "duration": 5.76}, {"text": "fair redress and guarantee of non", "start": 896.72, "duration": 7.16}, {"text": "repetition.", "start": 900.88, "duration": 3.0}, {"text": "Sriraelon stands with Africa, the", "start": 906.32, "duration": 4.879}, {"text": "Caribbean, and the wider African", "start": 909.04, "duration": 6.4}, {"text": "diaspora in advancing this cause,", "start": 911.199, "duration": 7.681}, {"text": "not to remain captive to the past, but", "start": 915.44, "duration": 6.399}, {"text": "to build a more just and equitable", "start": 918.88, "duration": 5.519}, {"text": "future.", "start": 921.839, "duration": 5.761}, {"text": "Mr. President, the same principle of", "start": 924.399, "duration": 5.761}, {"text": "fairness applies to Africa's critical", "start": 927.6, "duration": 5.56}, {"text": "minerals.", "start": 930.16, "duration": 3.0}, {"text": "Critical minerals are indispensable to", "start": 933.199, "duration": 5.281}, {"text": "the global energy transition.", "start": 935.6, "duration": 5.28}, {"text": "Yet too much value is still added", "start": 938.48, "duration": 4.479}, {"text": "elsewhere.", "start": 940.88, "duration": 6.16}, {"text": "Processing at source, fear value chains,", "start": 942.959, "duration": 7.761}, {"text": "technology transfer, and local industry", "start": 947.04, "duration": 7.599}, {"text": "would turn natural wealth into ski work,", "start": 950.72, "duration": 7.039}, {"text": "stronger economies, and hope for our", "start": 954.639, "duration": 5.681}, {"text": "young people.", "start": 957.759, "duration": 5.041}, {"text": "The green trans transition must not", "start": 960.32, "duration": 5.36}, {"text": "reproduce the extractive time of the", "start": 962.8, "duration": 5.2}, {"text": "past.", "start": 965.68, "duration": 6.56}, {"text": "For the youth, this is immediate.", "start": 968.0, "duration": 7.44}, {"text": "A young person without work,", "start": 972.24, "duration": 5.36}, {"text": "opportunity or a stake in the future", "start": 975.44, "duration": 5.92}, {"text": "becomes vulnerable to the recruiter, the", "start": 977.6, "duration": 6.239}, {"text": "smuggler and the dangerous journey", "start": 981.36, "duration": 5.2}, {"text": "across the Mediterranean.", "start": 983.839, "duration": 5.44}, {"text": "Jobs, skills, and dignity are therefore", "start": 986.56, "duration": 6.0}, {"text": "part of any serious policy for peace and", "start": 989.279, "duration": 5.201}, {"text": "development.", "start": 992.56, "duration": 4.079}, {"text": "Mr. President,", "start": 994.48, "duration": 5.599}, {"text": "Srielon does not ask the world", "start": 996.639, "duration": 7.361}, {"text": "what it does not demand of itself. We", "start": 1000.079, "duration": 6.32}, {"text": "carry these same principles into our", "start": 1004.0, "duration": 6.079}, {"text": "work at home. Through feed salon, we are", "start": 1006.399, "duration": 6.24}, {"text": "increasing domestic food production and", "start": 1010.079, "duration": 5.44}, {"text": "strengthening food security.", "start": 1012.639, "duration": 5.44}, {"text": "Through free quality education, we are", "start": 1015.519, "duration": 5.361}, {"text": "widening the path for the circumstances", "start": 1018.079, "duration": 8.801}, {"text": "of a child's birth. From a child's birth", "start": 1020.88, "duration": 12.0}, {"text": "to the future that awaits that child.", "start": 1026.88, "duration": 7.919}, {"text": "In 2024,", "start": 1032.88, "duration": 4.319}, {"text": "we enacted the prohibition of child", "start": 1034.799, "duration": 5.601}, {"text": "marriage act and subsequently championed", "start": 1037.199, "duration": 7.441}, {"text": "the proclamation of 27 November as the", "start": 1040.4, "duration": 6.399}, {"text": "international day for the elimination of", "start": 1044.64, "duration": 7.64}, {"text": "child Ali and forced marriage.", "start": 1046.799, "duration": 5.481}, {"text": "A girl in Sri Leon is no more or less", "start": 1052.799, "duration": 6.961}, {"text": "precious than a car anywhere else in our", "start": 1056.64, "duration": 5.919}, {"text": "beautiful world. protecting her", "start": 1059.76, "duration": 6.56}, {"text": "childhood, education and freedom as part", "start": 1062.559, "duration": 8.24}, {"text": "of what development is supposed to mean.", "start": 1066.32, "duration": 7.359}, {"text": "A gas future like the future of every", "start": 1070.799, "duration": 5.601}, {"text": "young person will be shaped by forces", "start": 1073.679, "duration": 5.921}, {"text": "already remake remaking our world.", "start": 1076.4, "duration": 6.32}, {"text": "Climate change, artificial intelligence", "start": 1079.6, "duration": 7.0}, {"text": "and the energy transition.", "start": 1082.72, "duration": 3.88}, {"text": "The meaning", "start": 1086.96, "duration": 5.12}, {"text": "of for all becomes more urgent as we", "start": 1088.799, "duration": 6.321}, {"text": "decide how these transformations will be", "start": 1092.08, "duration": 4.64}, {"text": "governed.", "start": 1095.12, "duration": 3.919}, {"text": "Artificial intelligence can improve of", "start": 1096.72, "duration": 5.839}, {"text": "course education, health, agriculture", "start": 1099.039, "duration": 6.321}, {"text": "and public administration.", "start": 1102.559, "duration": 5.681}, {"text": "It can also widen the inequality if", "start": 1105.36, "duration": 5.439}, {"text": "infrastructure, knowledge and rule", "start": 1108.24, "duration": 5.92}, {"text": "making remains concentrated in a few", "start": 1110.799, "duration": 5.601}, {"text": "countries.", "start": 1114.16, "duration": 4.879}, {"text": "Developing nations must help shape the", "start": 1116.4, "duration": 5.68}, {"text": "standards that will govern technologies", "start": 1119.039, "duration": 6.321}, {"text": "affecting their people.", "start": 1122.08, "duration": 5.599}, {"text": "Climate change presents the same moral", "start": 1125.36, "duration": 5.679}, {"text": "question in harsher form.", "start": 1127.679, "duration": 8.481}, {"text": "Who benefits? Who decides and who pays?", "start": 1131.039, "duration": 8.0}, {"text": "In Shen on Srielon's southern coast,", "start": 1136.16, "duration": 6.24}, {"text": "families watch the sea take their land,", "start": 1139.039, "duration": 6.321}, {"text": "fishing grounds and the graves of their", "start": 1142.4, "duration": 4.88}, {"text": "ancestors.", "start": 1145.36, "duration": 3.84}, {"text": "For them, climate change is the", "start": 1147.28, "duration": 6.24}, {"text": "disappearance of home in the present.", "start": 1149.2, "duration": 7.28}, {"text": "Those who contributed least", "start": 1153.52, "duration": 5.2}, {"text": "to the climate crisis are bearing some", "start": 1156.48, "duration": 4.4}, {"text": "of its gravest", "start": 1158.72, "duration": 5.12}, {"text": "greatest cost.", "start": 1160.88, "duration": 5.52}, {"text": "Accessible and predictable climate", "start": 1163.84, "duration": 5.68}, {"text": "finance, support for adaptation and", "start": 1166.4, "duration": 5.519}, {"text": "effective arrangement for loss and", "start": 1169.52, "duration": 7.44}, {"text": "damage are obligations of justice.", "start": 1171.919, "duration": 7.521}, {"text": "They are also investment in global", "start": 1176.96, "duration": 4.56}, {"text": "stability.", "start": 1179.44, "duration": 5.2}, {"text": "Fairness in trans transformation depends", "start": 1181.52, "duration": 7.44}, {"text": "on the institutions that govern it.", "start": 1184.64, "duration": 7.76}, {"text": "Syrielon therefore supports the UNH", "start": 1188.96, "duration": 5.52}, {"text": "initiative", "start": 1192.4, "duration": 4.24}, {"text": "and wider reforms that make this", "start": 1194.48, "duration": 5.92}, {"text": "organization more effective, accountable", "start": 1196.64, "duration": 6.399}, {"text": "and responsive.", "start": 1200.4, "duration": 5.36}, {"text": "Efficiency matters and reform must", "start": 1203.039, "duration": 6.481}, {"text": "preserve the capacity to act.", "start": 1205.76, "duration": 6.159}, {"text": "Mr. President,", "start": 1209.52, "duration": 4.48}, {"text": "the choice of the next Secretary General", "start": 1211.919, "duration": 5.12}, {"text": "offers another test of institutional", "start": 1214.0, "duration": 7.799}, {"text": "effectiveness and equality.", "start": 1217.039, "duration": 4.76}, {"text": "In 80 years, every Secretary General has", "start": 1222.64, "duration": 7.399}, {"text": "been a man.", "start": 1226.48, "duration": 3.559}, {"text": "The women put forward for this office", "start": 1235.2, "duration": 5.04}, {"text": "have placed their competence beyond", "start": 1237.679, "duration": 4.801}, {"text": "dispute.", "start": 1240.24, "duration": 4.799}, {"text": "What remains is the will of the", "start": 1242.48, "duration": 5.52}, {"text": "organization to live", "start": 1245.039, "duration": 6.161}, {"text": "by the quality equality it asks of", "start": 1248.0, "duration": 6.32}, {"text": "others and entrust a woman with his", "start": 1251.2, "duration": 6.599}, {"text": "highest office.", "start": 1254.32, "duration": 3.479}, {"text": "Mr. President,", "start": 1259.919, "duration": 4.88}, {"text": "our insistence on a capable United", "start": 1262.08, "duration": 6.24}, {"text": "Nations comes from experience", "start": 1264.799, "duration": 6.081}, {"text": "for Syrian. This organization is part of", "start": 1268.32, "duration": 5.52}, {"text": "our living history. It stood with us", "start": 1270.88, "duration": 6.159}, {"text": "when our country was broken and helped", "start": 1273.84, "duration": 7.04}, {"text": "us make peace durable.", "start": 1277.039, "duration": 7.201}, {"text": "In this hall, a small state has the same", "start": 1280.88, "duration": 7.279}, {"text": "vote as a great power. Imperfect as it", "start": 1284.24, "duration": 6.64}, {"text": "is, that quality remains one of", "start": 1288.159, "duration": 6.64}, {"text": "humanity's boldest promises.", "start": 1290.88, "duration": 6.08}, {"text": "Syria will continue to contribute", "start": 1294.799, "duration": 4.561}, {"text": "passionate to United Nations peace", "start": 1296.96, "duration": 5.52}, {"text": "operations, uphold international law,", "start": 1299.36, "duration": 5.679}, {"text": "support mediation and peace building,", "start": 1302.48, "duration": 4.88}, {"text": "defend the rights of women and girls,", "start": 1305.039, "duration": 5.361}, {"text": "and serve as a bridge", "start": 1307.36, "duration": 6.559}, {"text": "wherever member states seek one.", "start": 1310.4, "duration": 6.159}, {"text": "We will also continue to to support the", "start": 1313.919, "duration": 6.321}, {"text": "institutions of international justice.", "start": 1316.559, "duration": 6.721}, {"text": "In this regard, Srira Leon has nominated", "start": 1320.24, "duration": 8.6}, {"text": "Professor Charles Cho Jalo,", "start": 1323.28, "duration": 5.56}, {"text": "a distinguished international jurist", "start": 1329.6, "duration": 6.8}, {"text": "for to be endorsed by and has been", "start": 1333.2, "duration": 6.8}, {"text": "endorsed by the African Union and Echoas", "start": 1336.4, "duration": 6.08}, {"text": "for election as a judge of the", "start": 1340.0, "duration": 5.2}, {"text": "International Court of Justice.", "start": 1342.48, "duration": 5.6}, {"text": "We respectfully seek member state", "start": 1345.2, "duration": 7.479}, {"text": "support on the 3rd of November.", "start": 1348.08, "duration": 4.599}, {"text": "Mr. President, the United Nation was", "start": 1354.159, "duration": 6.081}, {"text": "created in a world of une unequal power,", "start": 1356.4, "duration": 8.08}, {"text": "yet it rests on a radical idea.", "start": 1360.24, "duration": 7.2}, {"text": "Nations differ in size and strength, but", "start": 1364.48, "duration": 5.92}, {"text": "their people do not differ in human", "start": 1367.44, "duration": 4.8}, {"text": "worth.", "start": 1370.4, "duration": 4.88}, {"text": "A united nation that delivers for all", "start": 1372.24, "duration": 5.76}, {"text": "makes that quality felt beyond this", "start": 1375.28, "duration": 4.72}, {"text": "hall.", "start": 1378.0, "duration": 5.039}, {"text": "Nearly 25 years ago, Syrian placed their", "start": 1380.0, "duration": 6.159}, {"text": "trust in peace because they believed", "start": 1383.039, "duration": 5.601}, {"text": "tomorrow could be different.", "start": 1386.159, "duration": 4.561}, {"text": "People around the world are asking", "start": 1388.64, "duration": 6.08}, {"text": "something similar of us. Now they need", "start": 1390.72, "duration": 6.48}, {"text": "reason to believe that cooperation still", "start": 1394.72, "duration": 6.24}, {"text": "works, that law still matters, and that", "start": 1397.2, "duration": 7.12}, {"text": "promises made here will be honored in", "start": 1400.96, "duration": 6.8}, {"text": "their lives. Let this session give them", "start": 1404.32, "duration": 6.76}, {"text": "that reason.", "start": 1407.76, "duration": 3.32}, {"text": "The words for all should not remain at", "start": 1413.12, "duration": 6.96}, {"text": "the end of this year's theme.", "start": 1416.24, "duration": 6.72}, {"text": "that must become the measure", "start": 1420.08, "duration": 5.2}, {"text": "of our work.", "start": 1422.96, "duration": 6.04}, {"text": "I thank you all.", "start": 1425.28, "duration": 3.72}, {"text": "On behalf of the assembly, I wish thank", "start": 1435.28, "duration": 5.519}, {"text": "to the president of the republic of", "start": 1437.76, "duration": 5.52}, {"text": "Srira Leon.", "start": 1440.799, "duration": 2.481}]